  "observations": [
    "Final ordinary native reference passes 141 checks/26 complete images, final C transport/shared-cache suite 308/26, and unchanged previous list client 108/26. Both browser list suites pass 34/13; Chromium button/text passes 107/48 and Firefox 108/48. Scoped total is 840 checks/200 complete images. All 35 existing provider/transport regression sections pass separately.",
    "The real 180x96 native list reports clip (21,2,157,92), unscrolled client (176,92), and maximum y 268 for the tested 24-row model. These are observations, never constants used by an adapter. The ordinary empty list even has a native y limit of 8, which consumers must not replace with an invented empty-list rule.",
    "Actual previous 568-byte provider fallback is exercised through both C API and IPC. Generic geometry is unavailable while original list models and pixels remain usable. Read queries do not add selection actions; other connections cannot read geometry for the creating owner.",
    "Shared cache scrolling and wheel calls retain native state/geometry/pixels without adding selection actions. Existing native text geometry and the generic entry return identical measured fields.",
    "Only isolated candidate SDK and small browser adapters/probes are built. Existing production components, prior shared SDK and prior browser adapters retain their hashes. Real content renderers retain Seccomp=2 and NoNewPrivs=1. All owned fixtures are stopped with no candidate mappings.",
    "Geometry measurement and transport are a dependency for full browser scrolling. They do not establish native DOM option layout, intrinsic sizing, script scroll synchronization or wheel/default ownership."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Consume native clip/document/limits in both original browser layout/scroll models, with original trusted scroll lifecycle, script/native offset synchronization, option geometry and intrinsic sizing.",
    "Complete list wheel/APZ/default routing, held-scroller repaint/echo, selection reveal ownership and host/session replacement replay.",
    "Broader models/CSS/transforms/zoom/mixed-DPI, IME/accessibility/focus traversal, other browser builds/derivatives and installed deployment.",
    "Remaining browser controls, complete detached menus and native shortcuts, then GTK/Qt/KDE using the same shared layer. Browser toolbar/address bar/tabs remain original."
  ],
